hc_faqs=[('Who decides who we interview?','You do. You know which patient, which nurse and which donor carries the story, and we do not. Give us the names and we handle everything after that.'),('How do you handle patient consent?','A signed release before anyone is on camera, on your forms if your compliance team prefers them. Nothing is filmed, edited or published without one, and a participant who withdraws later comes out of every deliverable at no charge.'),('What exactly is a quote library?','Every usable line from every interview, transcribed, attributed and sorted by theme. Your writers stop scrubbing through footage looking for the sentence they half remember.'),('Can one project serve the campaign and recruiting?','Yes, and most should. The same interviews carry both, because the reason someone gives and the reason someone stays are usually the same reason.'),('Do you need our facilities or crew?','Neither. We bring the crew, the lighting and the sound, and we work in the rooms you already have.'),('What if the campaign timeline slips?','It usually does, and it does not affect the footage. Interviews filmed now are just as usable at the kickoff, the gala and the close, which is why the timing argument runs the other way.')]
